// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Moss_Bat_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P586926391" "Moss Bats are the weakest of the creatures infecteed by the Tellurian spores.  They spread the Tellurian plague by darting in to bite unsuspecting victims, and then quickly flying out of reach."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Fungoid_LT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1871086507" "Fungoids have a simple intelligence, seemingly designed only to spread the Tellurian infection.  They can release noxious Spore Clouds that can spread infection rapidly."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Fungoid_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Fungoid_Spore_Cloud 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3311183004" "Fungoid Spore Clouds spread infection, bringing more under the will of the Hamidon."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Rotters_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1814962174" "These once living trees have been infested with Tellurian Spores, granting them mobility and a vicious nature.  Its thick rotting hide splinters as it moves, dropping needle sharp shards of bark.  When attacked, splinters fly in all directions, damaging anything nearby and infecting them with the plague."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Rotters_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Rotters_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Rotvine_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2795615920" "This cluster of animated foliage wields a hideous array of razor sharp leaves.  While more intelligent and vicious then other Tellurian creatures, Devoured Rotvines are still mere plague spreaders for the Hamidon.  Infected pustules grow around Rotvines, constantly bursting and releasing clouds of toxic spores into the air."
// DisplayNames :
"P129843915" "Devoured Rotvine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Rotvine_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Rotvine_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Foulbriar_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P821426159" "The shriveled musculature and thorn-like portrusions of the Devoured Foulbriar hide what was once a human infected by the Tellurian plague.  These lost souls command ropy tendrils that can immobilize and hold the toughest of Heroes and Villains."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Foulbriar_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Foulbriar_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Mirebark_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P393340474" "As the tellurian infection gains complete control of its human hosts brain, they become even more vicious and cunning.  Devoured Mirebark can move extremely quickly, and can feel the vibrations of anything moving over the ground and in the air."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Mirebark_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Greater_Devoured_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2268775346" "The most advanced cases of fungal infection, Greater Devoured are tremendously strong and tough.  They have direct control over the ground around them, covering themselves in protective soil and creating mudpots of Tellurian spores."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - DevouringEarthPraetorian_Thorn_Spitter 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2086846922" "Thorn Spitter's hide underground with only the tip of a tendril above ground to sense when anything moves nearby.  If anyone passes near a Thorn Spitter, it will erupt out of the ground and fling poisonous spines at its enemies. If no one is nearby, it goes back to a dormant state again, hiding for the next unsuspecting foe."
// DisplayNames :
"P675782090" "Thorn Spitter"

