// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_SpiritGuide 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2898263663" "This creature's grisly appearance is not unlike a hundred different descriptions of the grim reaper or the ferryman. Indeed, a spirit guide's existence is devoted to the ushering of souls from one world to the next. They do so with mechanical efficiency and enthusiasm, as their reward for a job well done is a payment in wax, which keeps their spirit candle burning, if only long enough to find another soul in need of guidance to the next world."
// DisplayNames :
"P552045883" "Spirit Guide"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_HoodedLantern 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P504120621" "The Drudges' Hooded Lanterns are powered by the wax of souls which they collect and use as currency.  This torch flickers and floats before you, moving at the whim of the Taskmasters who control the Drudges' heirarchy."
// DisplayNames :
"P2221381527" "Hooded Lantern"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_HoodedLantern_Summoned 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Patrolman 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P685251757" "In the Night Ward the Drudge Patrolmen are the embodiment of the authority and law of the Taskmaster's Office. Some souls try to resist their transition from one world to the next, while outsiders are always trafficking in stolen souls. It is the Patrolman's job to ensure that operations in Night Ward move smoothly, and take care of any complications that might arise."
// DisplayNames :
"P715541474" "Patrolman"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Lamplighter 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P843638907" "Lamplighters are tasked with keeping Night Ward's lamps lit and push back the dark forces that hunger for the souls of the dead. However, their spiritual flame is more than just for lighting lamps, it can also ignite one's soul."
// DisplayNames :
"P3415793957" "Lamplighter"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Watcher 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2593121611" "The Watchers oversee squads of Patrolmen and are assigned by Drudge Taskmasters to act as cudgels when something needs to be done quickly and efficiently. They are feared not only because of their lash, but because they can call upon the very shadows of Night Ward to hunt down those who obstruct the directives of the Taskmaster's Office."
// DisplayNames :
"P2100485936" "Watcher"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Taskmaster 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2050354023" "Taskmasters are the bureaucratic masterminds of the Drudges. They have, for time immemorial,  been in charge of the flow of souls from each world to the next, and they have made a great deal of profit off of their services. The Taskmasters deal in wax, which is used to keep the candles of the Drudges burning - but in order to meet the demands of their Taskmasters the Drudges must burn their candles at both ends, creating an eternal cycle of dependence."
// DisplayNames :
"P801658810" "Taskmaster"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Burn 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// GroupDescription :
"P142474770" "Fire Armor"
// DisplayNames :
"P638756335" "Flames"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Radiance_Jump1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// GroupDescription :
"P3934056204" "Radiance"
// DisplayNames :
"P831892720" "Radiance Jump 1"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Radiance_Jump2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2828860746" "Radiance Jump 2"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Radiance_Jump3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3751529948" "Radiance Jump 3"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_LightThePath 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// GroupDescription :
"P2072399166" "Light the Path"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Soul_Beast 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3455608068" "The Soul Beast are deadly beasts of the Netherworld who accompany the Drudges in their unending task of transitioning souls from one world to the next."
// DisplayNames :
"P2849871108" "Soul Beast"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Drudges_Shade 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3258115219" "These netherworld horrors hunger for the essence of the living.  Once their victims have been chosen their assault will cease only once their appetites have been sated."
// DisplayNames :
"P845088649" "Shade"

